WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.408
OT telemetry is the foundation of visibility into industrial systems.

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:15.047
It includes network communication, process values, device and controller events, endpoint logs, alarms, identities, remote sessions, and configuration changes.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:19.985
Each source answers different questions and carries different limitations.

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:22.571
Useful telemetry combines layers.

00:00:22.571 --> 00:00:26.568
Network data shows paths and protocol behavior.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:31.035
Process data shows physical conditions and control response.

00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:36.913
Endpoint and system logs identify users, files, services, and local changes.

00:00:36.913 --> 00:00:44.202
Protocol context explains industrial operations, while asset and maintenance context explains why they matter.

00:00:44.202 --> 00:00:46.788
Safe collection is essential.

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:58.308
Passive observation and existing logs are often preferred near sensitive systems, and any new agent, query, or configuration should be tested with engineering.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:03.246
Visibility must not undermine reliability, availability, or process integrity.

00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:10.534
Quality requires completeness, accuracy, synchronized time, useful retention, normalization, asset mapping, and honest coverage.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:15.942
Blind spots and noisy data should be measured and managed.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:22.760
Collection alone is not success if teams cannot trust or interpret the result.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:30.519
Security operations use telemetry for detection, hunting, incident response, anomaly analysis, inventory, and vulnerability prioritization.

00:01:30.519 --> 00:01:41.570
The strongest programs connect those workflows with operators and engineers, turn findings into improvements, and continually align evidence with the real architecture.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:49.328
OT telemetry does not replace operational judgment; it gives that judgment a stronger factual foundation.
